Subject: [flux] Reserve grit resource ids for the chrome://flux console

grit refuses to build a .grd it has no id range for:

  Exception: Please update gen\tools\gritsettings\default_resource_ids and add
  a first id for .../chrome/browser/resources/flux/resources.grd (includes).

The integers are fake start ids - only their relative order matters, per
tools/gritsettings/README.md - so flux takes 3990, between feedback (3980) and
gaia_auth_host (4000). That keeps it alphabetical in the same place patch 0005
puts it in chrome_paks.gni and //chrome/browser/resources. They overlap the
next range on paper and that is fine: actual ids are assigned dynamically, and
for a generated .grd the only real constraint is sizes.

sizes.includes is what bounds it, and it is a HARD bound. Exceeding it fails
the build with:

  grit.exception.IdRangeOverflow: Generated .grd file used more IDs (23) than
  were allocated for it (20) for type includes.

which lands about 500 targets in, on a machine that cannot afford the round
trip. It was 20, sized against the 7 resources the console had at the time;
the console reached 23 (7 static files, 15 compiled .ts, the mojom bindings)
and tipped it over.

60 now, matching glic, which is the closest thing to a peer in this file. The
count to check it against is len(static_files) + len(ts_files) + len(mojo_files)
in src/resources/BUILD.gn - tools/check-webui.sh asserts it so this cannot be
discovered by a build again.

--- a/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
+++ b/tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec
@@ -513,6 +513,10 @@
     "META": {"sizes": {"includes": [40],}},
     "includes": [3980],
   },
+  "<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/chrome/browser/resources/flux/resources.grd": {
+    "META": {"sizes": {"includes": [60],}},
+    "includes": [3990],
+  },
   "<(SHARED_INTERMEDIATE_DIR)/chrome/browser/resources/gaia_auth_host/resources.grd": {
     "META": {"sizes": {"includes": [20],}},
     "includes": [4000],
